# The §22B-1e1 failing-first baseline, verbatim from the editor log.
#
# Run before anything was recorded:
#
#   scripts/run_identity_measurement.sh --expect-stable --runs 1
#
# `--expect-stable` asserts the optimistic contract, that every tracked
# reference still means the same FerriteCAD object after the reimport. Unity
# 6000.4.10f1 exited 1 on the first scenario. Stack-trace lines are omitted:
# they name line numbers in a version of the probe that no longer exists, and
# the message is the measurement.

FCAD_FBX_IDENTITY_FAILURE System.InvalidOperationException: a saved reference stopped meaning the same FerriteCAD object: s01-byte-identical-reimport mesh:definition=step.product_definition#50 -> retargeted_to_another_definition

# That first failure was the probe's, not Unity's: it compared managed object
# references, and a reimport hands back a different C# instance for the same
# persisted object. The corrected probe compares the pair a project file
# actually stores, and answers `same_semantic` for every reference in scenario
# one. The failure is kept because the fix for it changed what this
# measurement is allowed to conclude.
#
# The earlier refusal, from the run before that, was the other half of the same
# defect: Unity sorts an imported hierarchy by name after the custom-property
# callbacks have run, so the durable keys landed on the wrong finished objects.
# It is recorded here in the same verbatim form.

